{"text": "Monday to Wednesday.\n\nGrandpa Kemal is seventy-two. He lives in Ankara.\n\nHe has a small flat. He has a big laugh. And he has a new phone. It is black and thin.\n\nThis week, Grandpa has one job. On Saturday, it is Ece's birthday. Ece is his granddaughter.\n\nGrandpa wants to send her one nice photo. It is easy, right?\n\nBut the new phone does everything wrong.\n\nToday is Monday. Saturday is five days away.\n\nOn Monday morning, Grandpa sits on his sofa. He looks at the phone. The phone looks at him.\n\n\"Call Ece,\" he says to the phone.\n\nThe phone rings. Then a man answers.\n\n\"Good morning! This is the bread shop!\"\n\n\"The bread shop?\" says Grandpa. \"No, no. Sorry!\"\n\nThe man laughs. \"Kemal, is that you? Your big cake is ready!\"\n\n\"What cake?\" asks Grandpa. But the call ends.\n\n\"Oh no,\" he says.\n\nOn Tuesday, Grandpa opens his window. The city is beautiful today.\n\nHe can see Mert's window. Mert is fourteen. He lives on the same floor. His window has a blue curtain.\n\nToday Mert's flat is full of noise. Many people laugh in there.\n\nGrandpa wants a photo of the city. He touches the phone. But the photo is not the city. It is his foot!\n\n\"Oh no!\" says Grandpa.\n\nThen the phone makes a happy noise. Where is the photo now? Grandpa does not know.\n\nOn Wednesday, Grandpa goes to the park. He sits with his friends. They drink tea and play a game.\n\nThen music comes from his pocket. Dance music! Birds fly up. Everyone looks at Grandpa.\n\nHe touches everything. The music does not stop. Now he has photos of his ear. And the sky.\n\nHis friends laugh. \"Kemal, is that your new phone?\"\n\n\"Yes,\" says Grandpa. \"My new phone hates me.\"\n\nIn the evening, the phone rings. It is Ece! He touches the red button.\n\nThe call ends.\n\n\"Oh no! Ece!\"", "textSha256": "e1b00882d093f79ff767e22bfc2515f698a5b11276022f461640a234a03b591c", "voice_id": "EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "speed": 0.9, "lang": "en", "parts": 1, "a